====>Introduction to the Version Control System :
---------------------------------------------
-Version Control System is also known as software configuration management(SCM) or Source code management System(SCM).

--> Need of SCM or VCS :
--------------------
-we should not overwrite our code.
-Every version we have to maintain.
 1)maintaining multiple version manually is very complex activity.

 2)Developer-A and Developer-B working on the code . At last we have to merge the code developed by both developers and we have to deliver it to client . if both the developers developed a file named util.java,then one copy will overwrite another ,which creates abnormal behaviour . we should not overwrite our code.
 
 3)Every change should be tracked like :
                who did the change 
                when he did the change 
                which changes he did etc...
   and all changes should be maintained.
  
  4)Overwriting of the code should not be happened.

  5)Developers have to share their code to peer developers , so that multiple developers will work in collaboration way.
  
  6)Parallel development must be required.

--->How Version Control System Works :
---------------------------------------
-version control System (VCS)  always talks about files which contain source code.
-Everyone required VCS to maintain different versions of their documents.
-developer==>to maintain the  different versions of the code.
-Tester==>to maintain different versions of the test scripts.
-Architect==>to maintain different versions of documents.
-Project Manager==>to maintain different versions of Excel sheets..etc...

Basic terminology of VCS :
---------------------------
-->working directory :
----------------------
-where developers are required to create/modify files.
-here version control is not applicable. Here we won't use the work to maintain like version-1 , version-2...

-->Repository: 
---------------
-where we have to store files and metadata.
-Here version control is applicable.
-Here we can talk versions like version-1 version-2 etc....

-->Commit :-It is process of sending files from working directory to the repository.
----------

Checkout :-The process of sending files from repository to working directory.
----------

Benefits of VCS :
----------------
1)We can maintain different versions and we can choose any version based on client requirement.
2)With Every version/commit we can maintain metadata like :
      -commit message
      -who did the change 
      -when did he change
      -what changes he did
3)Developers can share the code to their peer developers in very easy way.
4)Multiple developers can work in collaborative way.
5)Parallel Development
6)we can provide access control like :
      - who can read code.
      - who can modify code.
